      {
        "slide": 6,
        "role": "evidence",
        "subject": "Two matte dark green stock tanks seated in a containment wall, joined by a walkway that the tanks and a stair carry. A pale float gauge board with ten tick marks runs the full shell height of the near tank, and an orange target rides the board just under its midpoint.",
        "visual_consequence": "With no number printed, the gauge carries the share by itself. The target sits at about 0.47 of the board's height, so a reader sees a tank gauged a little under half, and the hook says exactly that.",
        "weakness": "Polish only. The scene, lighting and materials are identical to the bound readings. The target is the only accent and reads at 432 px. Without a label, under rather than at half rests on about one tick-width at feed size, and the dek's 'that share' has a loose referent. The bound notes stand: a hard value step at some weld seams, even shell lighting, no visible cast from the target, a dark wall face for the lower third.",
        "repair": "None required before the remaining frames. Optional polish: make the middle tick visibly longer so a reader sees at a glance that the target sits just under half.",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
        "feed_legible": true,
