      {
        "slide": 9,
        "role": "close",
        "subject": "A worker in a hard hat and hi-vis vest, seen from behind with hands on hips, stands at a closed ranch gate in warm-lit grass. Beyond the gate the pump jack works on the far side of the caliche lease road.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline a reader sees a person on the outside of a closed gate looking at the machine. That is the deck's open question about who checks what the watcher finds, made literal. The new dek gives that question a dated next step.",
        "weakness": "The warm rim light lands mainly on the ground rather than the walking beam and horsehead, which keep only a thin cool sliver, so the panel's unlit-silhouette charge still stands. The brighter grass seats the worker but raises the ground behind the claim ids, which stay legible. The worker is still cut at the shins and the cattle guard is below the frame edge.",
        "repair": "Not an audition blocker. Re-aim the warm light behind the jack nearly opposite the camera at 10 to 20 degrees elevation, kept off the ground, so it grazes the horsehead face and the beam's upper edge.",
